It is Saturday morning, and I am at the café.
I have just wiped down the counter.
My shift is over, and I untie my apron.
I have gotten off early today.
Last weekend I had a long shift.
But today the shift has been quiet.
We were not busy at all.
I am really looking forward to tonight.
It is my first Danish summer.
I take out my phone.
I write a message to Nina.
We have planned to see a big bonfire.
"I am already finished at the café," I write to her.
"Are we still meeting at eight o'clock?"
Nina replies almost immediately.
"Yes, we are!"
"I am looking forward to it," she writes back.
I smile, take my bag, and walk out into the sun.
